From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0012] mil_infer: deploy-gate decoder probes (PROBE-2)

Two fork-isolated probe binaries used to decode the _ANEClient deploy gate:

- examples/dp3.rs — loads one HWX/Mach-O/bundle through
  EspressoProgram::load_precompiled and reports which stage failed
  (modelAtURL parse vs loadModel deploy) plus the hex error code.
- examples/deploy_probe.rs — same load, prints LOAD_OK / LOAD_FAIL code.

These are how the error codes in docs/evidence/0010-deploy-gate-codes.md were
measured. Each runs as its own process because ObjC exceptions abort (the
Apple shipped .H17 bundles crash the loader).

No library code changed — examples only.

Stacking: apply after 0001..0011.
Upstream: 20f097fb34969cd577342a4d7996fbf5464998c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/mil_infer/examples/dp3.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+// FORK(ane-stack) PROBE-2: separate modelAtURL (parse) from loadModel (deploy).
+use mil_infer::espresso::EspressoProgram;
+use std::path::Path;
+fn main() {
+    let p = std::env::args().nth(1).unwrap();
+    // load_precompiled does modelAtURL then loadModel; the Err message tells us which failed.
+    match EspressoProgram::load_precompiled(Path::new(&p), &[]) {
+        Ok(_) => println!("RESULT: LOAD_OK"),
+        Err(e) => {
+            let s = format!("{e:?}");
+            if s.contains("modelAtURL") { println!("RESULT: FAIL_AT_modelAtURL: {s}"); }
+            else if s.contains("loadModel") {
+                let code = s.find("0x").map(|i| s[i..].chars().take(8).collect::<String>()).unwrap_or("none".into());
+                println!("RESULT: FAIL_AT_loadModel code={code}");
+            } else { println!("RESULT: FAIL_OTHER: {s}"); }
+        }
+    }
+}
